    {
      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-guts-2016-p13.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Answer: \\(48+\\sqrt{2016}\\)\nThere are no integer solutions to \\(a^{2}+b^{2}=2016\\) due to the presence of the prime 7 on the right-hand side (by Fermat's Christmas Theorem). Assuming \\(a<b\\), the minimal solution \\((a, b)=(3,45)\\) which gives the answer above.",
